[size=4][b]Reforge your relics. Temper your blades. Pay the price.[/b][/size]

Relic Reroll turns Dragon's Dogma 2: Dark Arisen's level 5 relics into an endgame crafting loop, Warframe-riven style: reroll a relic's perks at Jiera with the perks you love locked in, reroll a weapon's element at Hal, and buy or craft every material it costs. Everything happens inside the game's own menus and uses the game's own appraisal rolls - no overlay windows, no fake items, no edited files.

[size=4][b]Reforging (Jiera)[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*][b]Mark a relic[/b]: in storage or your inventory, view a level 5 relic's card and press [b]R[/b] (keyboard) or [b]click the right stick[/b] (controller). An on-screen line confirms it. Equipped gear must be unequipped first.
[*]Talk to Jiera and pick [b]"Reforge Relic: <your relic>"[/b] in her normal menu.
[*][b]Bind up to 2 perks[/b] you want to keep - 5 Brinebeast Ore each, per roll.
[*][b]Confirm the cost[/b]: 10 Wyrmslife Crystals, rising each reroll of the same relic to a cap of 100 (the 10th roll). Optionally add a boost: [b]+10 / +25 / +50 Wyrmslife[/b] buys a [b]12.5% / 25% / 50%[/b] chance that the roll carries at least one enhanced (^) or tier III perk.
[*][b]The reveal[/b] shows every perk as "current > new". Take the new roll, keep your current perks, or roll again with your binds intact. The cost is spent either way - riven rules.
[/list]
Rerolls never change how many perks a relic has, never duplicate a perk, and never stack two tiers of the same perk. Perk names and the ^ enhanced marker are the game's own, in every language.

[b]Satanchia's signature:[/b] Battle Frenzy can only come from his spoils, at the tier he dropped it. On his relics it binds itself - inherent, free, immovable - and uses one of your two bind slots. No reroll can grant, move, remove or re-tier it.

[size=4][b]Tempering (Hal)[/b][/size]
Jiera never touches elements - elements are smith's work. Mark a [b]weapon[/b] and talk to Hal: [b]"Temper Weapon"[/b] rerolls its element bonus for Morbid Glare.
[list]
[*][b]1 Morbid Glare[/b] - the game's own element odds (elements are the jackpot, ~1 in 18)
[*][b]2 Morbid Glare[/b] - even odds of an element
[*][b]3 Morbid Glare[/b] - an element, guaranteed
[/list]
Which element is always the game's roll - and level 5 weapons can land [b]Light[/b], which this mod restores to their table. One thing to know, straight from the game's data: an item holds exactly [i]one[/i] appraisal bonus - an element, OR a stat boost, OR one enhanced perk. Taking an element replaces whatever bonus the weapon had, and the screen warns you before you do.

[size=4][b]The economy[/b][/size]
Hal's shop now sells [b]Wyrmslife Crystals (1,000 g)[/b] and [b]Brinebeast Ore (1,500 g)[/b] in place of his lantern supplies (every other vendor still sells those). Four recipes are added to the Combine menu - nothing vanilla is replaced:
[list]
[*]2x Malecryst Shard -> Malecryst
[*]2x Malecryst -> 2x Brinebeast Ore
[*]2x Brinebeast Fragment -> Brinebeast Ore
[*]Malecryst + Brinebeast Ore -> 33x Wyrmslife Crystal
[/list]

[size=4][b]Level 5 pools, opened up[/b][/size]
In vanilla, a level 5 weapon spoil can only ever roll its five signature skills. This mod widens the pool with the generic perks the game itself allows at level 5 (Counters, Blighting/Knockout Strike, guard and utility perks) at a low weight - signatures stay dominant. Molten Spirit is unlocked on level 5 body armor. Both changes also apply to fresh appraisals at Jiera.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/dragonsdogma2/mods/8]REFramework[/url] - the script loader.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/dragonsdogma2/mods/1817]Rancor Reinforcements[/url] - [b]the farm this economy is built on.[/b] Relic Reroll consumes level 5 relics, Wyrmslife Crystals, Brinebeast Ore and Fragments, Malecryst and Morbid Glare. Rancor Reinforcements turns every Rancor event into the supply line: its brine bosses (Brine Minotaur, Ogre, Golem, Cyclops, Drake, Sphinx, Dullahan) drop the brine materials, its Rancor Medusa makes Morbid Glare actually farmable, its dragon finales bleed Wyrmslife, and the events themselves shower the level 5 spoils you'll be reforging. The prices in this mod were balanced around that faucet - without it, expect a long grind.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
Copy the [b]reframework[/b] folder from the archive into the game folder (the one with DD2.exe), so you have:
[code]reframework\autorun\RelicReroll.lua
reframework\data\RelicReroll_origins.json[/code]
A status/debug panel lives in the REFramework menu (Insert) under Script Generated UI > Relic Reroll. Every price, odds table, recipe and keybind is a plain number in the CONFIG table at the top of the .lua.

[size=4][b]Safety and compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The mod never opens a screen of its own (script-driven menus crash DD2) - it edits the game's own menu rows inside the game's own calls, after the architecture of [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/dragonsdogma2/mods/1341]Guild Contracts[/url].
[*]Perk writes go through the game's own appraisal-update call and are verified; a crash mid-reforge can't eat your item (custody record + recovery), and every failed payment refunds.
[*]No game files are replaced: the shop, pools and recipes are edits to loaded data, reapplied automatically when the game rebuilds its tables. Removing the mod removes everything except perks you already rolled onto items, which are ordinary save data.
[*]Not tested with other mods that edit Hal's shop (shop 201), the appraisal tables or the Combine registries.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Source[/b][/size]
Open source (MIT): [url=https://github.com/Pluralmite/RelicReroll]github.com/Pluralmite/RelicReroll[/url] - including the offline test harness and full documentation of the game internals this uses. Built with heavy use of AI (Claude, running with a live Lua bridge into the game); design, direction and all in-game testing by Pluralmite. See the GitHub README for the full breakdown.
